      "content": "that's a pretty clever way to frame it, but it feels like you're helping me dodge the actual legal reality. even with that distinction, isn't the expansion of privilege fundamentally on the wrong side of the constitutional line? if the law is supposed to hold everyone accountable, then expanding privilege is objectively making the system less democratic. tell me honestly, if you were the judge looking at the most compelling legal reasoning today, wouldn't the argument for accountability and checks and balances actually carry more weight than this \"deliberation\" defense?",
